WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.792 --> 00:00:14.112
Wedding parents need their makeup to hold up, without breaking down, for at least about five hours from when it starts until the wedding ends.

2
00:00:14.448 --> 00:00:22.008
To achieve a natural skin finish, we apply thin layers multiple times.

3
00:00:22.344 --> 00:00:31.152
If dead skin cells are left on the surface, or fine lines stand out from dryness, a natural skin finish becomes difficult.

4
00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:40.224
Leftover dead skin makes foundation lift, and as time passes, dryness-related wrinkles become more visible.

5
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:51.624
Middle-aged skin, which regenerates more slowly and holds less moisture, needs care for dryness and exfoliation starting about two to three months before the wedding.

6
00:00:51.960 --> 00:01:04.056
Good skin condition helps foundation adhere and last longer, and it keeps fine lines from standing out when you're smiling brightly at guests on the day.

7
00:01:04.392 --> 00:01:16.752
A gentle exfoliant once a week removes buildup and helps prevent makeup from lifting, and patting toner in more than three times after cleansing, the patting technique, helps too.

8
00:01:17.088 --> 00:01:23.904
For menopausal redness in particular, a sterile saline mask can really help calm the skin.

9
00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:34.416
Skin cared for this carefully, once it meets a professional's touch, comes out looking radiant and luxurious, like glowing, dewy skin that feels like your own.

10
00:01:34.752 --> 00:01:38.976
Subtle glowing skin versus a greasy shine, what's the difference?

11
00:01:39.312 --> 00:01:46.440
The key to a luxurious wedding-parent look is that dewy, glowing skin finish.

12
00:01:46.776 --> 00:01:57.288
This is different from a greasy shine, it's a technique using a fine-particle shiny base that makes the skin glow softly under the lighting.

13
00:01:57.624 --> 00:02:05.352
But applying that glow across the entire face can make it look bigger, since the fine particles reflect light everywhere,

14
00:02:05.688 --> 00:02:12.840
so the technique focuses the glow on the T-zone and fades it out toward the edges of the face.

15
00:02:13.176 --> 00:02:19.632
The sides of the face are shaded instead, to create dimension and a slimmer look.

16
00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:25.752
Dewy, subtly glowing skin is what gives a wedding parent that luxurious look.
